🌸 Introduction

Welcome to my GitHub repository! ♡

This repository serves as my digital portfolio, where I organized and presented my activities, outputs, and projects in one accessible space. Through this activity, I learned how GitHub can be used not only for coding but also for organizing, documenting, and showcasing creative and academic work.

🎀 01 — Creating My Repository

To begin, I created a new repository on GitHub and gave it a clear and appropriate name for my digital portfolio.

After creating the repository, I prepared the basic structure and added a README.md file. The README serves as the introduction and main guide to the contents of my portfolio.

I also customized the README to make it more visually appealing, organized, and easy to navigate. ✨

🩷 02 — Uploading & Organizing My Activities

I uploaded my activities and outputs into the repository and organized them into separate sections so that each activity could be easily located.

My portfolio is divided into three main activities:

🎀 Activity	💗 Focus
Activity 1	GitHub Repository Setup & Portfolio
Activity 2	Color Palette & Typography
Activity 3	Social Media Infographics & Mini Project

I used clear file names and organized my materials carefully to avoid confusion and make the repository easier to understand.

💻 03 — Making My Digital Portfolio Presentable

To make my portfolio accessible and presentable, I focused on creating a clean structure and visually appealing README.

I used headings, tables, spacing, emojis, and visual elements to improve the overall appearance. I also made sure that my files were properly uploaded and that the content could be accessed through the repository.

My goal was to create a portfolio that was not only functional but also reflected my personal style and creativity. 🎀

✨ 04 — Challenges & Solutions

While setting up my GitHub repository, I encountered a few challenges.

💭 Challenge: Organizing my files

At first, it was difficult to decide how to arrange my activities and outputs.

♡ Solution:
I created a simple structure and grouped related files together. This made the repository easier to navigate.

💭 Challenge: Making the README visually appealing

A basic README looked too plain for a creative portfolio.

♡ Solution:
I used Markdown formatting, headings, tables, emojis, and visual elements to create a more engaging design.

💭 Challenge: Uploading and managing files

Uploading multiple files and making sure everything was properly placed required careful checking.

♡ Solution:
I reviewed the repository after uploading my files and corrected file names and organization when necessary.

💖 What I Learned

Through this activity, I learned how to:

🎀 Create and set up a GitHub repository
💻 Upload and manage files
📂 Organize digital outputs
✨ Use Markdown to create a presentable README
🌸 Document my work clearly
💗 Build a simple and accessible digital portfolio

Most importantly, I learned that GitHub can be used as a platform to showcase and document my creative work, not just store files.

